211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 106 0 R
/T (This project was done individually. From brainstorming, planning the website, the theme, to making the whole thing happen. But I did get some help from my friend who owned the business. And she helped me conceptualize, as well as confirm a few things. Without her permission, this website wouldn't have happened. Firstly, I learnt that this was definitely not a one man job. It was possible, however, it definitely made the whole process more challenging. Since all the responsibilities fell on me. The designing, coding, as well as the editing and making sure the website worked properly. Although, I did get help from AI inside Visual Code Studio, I still had to make sure that the codes were correct, and that the website was up to my own standards. Secondly, it was still a fun experience despite the hardships. Whenever I finished editing, I found myself looking forward to the results. I liked being able to test it out, and watching the website slowly build itself. Lastly, If I were to continue developing the Kooki Bakes platform, I would introduce these key enhancements. Firstly, I would build an interactive custom order calculator that allows users to select flavor combinations \(such as Matcha, S'mores, or Crinkles\) and preview tiered pricing before launching their social media inquiry. I would also add a dynamic batch availability indicator so customers can view daily baking schedules in real time. I would definitely try to get into Javascript to further improve this website. Obviously, there are still a few things missing in this website. It's not perfect, but it's a great start. It also made me curious about web design, and if I had the time I would definitely try to search more about it. It was a unique and fun experience, despite all the trial and errors.)
/E (This project was done individually. From brainstorming, planning the website, the theme, to making the whole thing happen. But I did get some help from my friend who owned the business. And she helped me conceptualize, as well as confirm a few things. Without her permission, this website wouldn't have happened. Firstly, I learnt that this was definitely not a one man job. It was possible, however, it definitely made the whole process more challenging. Since all the responsibilities fell on me. The designing, coding, as well as the editing and making sure the website worked properly. Although, I did get help from AI inside Visual Code Studio, I still had to make sure that the codes were correct, and that the website was up to my own standards. Secondly, it was still a fun experience despite the hardships. Whenever I finished editing, I found myself looking forward to the results. I liked being able to test it out, and watching the website slowly build itself. Lastly, If I were to continue developing the Kooki Bakes platform, I would introduce these key enhancements. Firstly, I would build an interactive custom order calculator that allows users to select flavor combinations \(such as Matcha, S'mores, or Crinkles\) and preview tiered pricing before launching their social media inquiry. I would also add a dynamic batch availability indicator so customers can view daily baking schedules in real time. I would definitely try to get into Javascript to further improve this website. Obviously, there are still a few things missing in this website. It's not perfect, but it's a great start. It also made me curious about web design, and if I had the time I would definitely try to search more about it. It was a unique and fun experience, despite all the trial and errors.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
